    "root": "Perceiving something a room had no language for yet earned a reputation for a specific quality of attention that ordinary expertise rarely produces, so people traveled toward that quality while telling themselves the reason was practical. People remembered the shift in their own thinking more than any specific advice given. That shift is what shaped the reputation.",
    "defaultMode": "Certainty about what you have seen, delivered without translation, reads as grandiosity, and the door closes before the content is heard. Practical colleagues quietly stop bringing you real problems because your answers arrive at an altitude nothing can be built at, and the fewer people who challenge you, the stranger the private thinking becomes.",
    "blindSpot": "You do not see how quickly practical colleagues stop bringing you real problems once your answers start arriving at a level nothing can actually be built at. What feels like insight offered generously reads to them as unusable.",
    "underusedStrength": "A reputation for a genuinely unusual quality of perception is rare and worth translating deliberately into something usable. Grounding one insight explicitly in a concrete, practical next step is what lets the reputation include being useful instead of only being unworldly."
