    "root": "Catching the exact wrong word before it became expensive earned a reputation that general competence rarely produces, so precision attached to your name as something specific rather than diffuse. People remembered the one thing that did not go wrong because you read it. That specificity is what shaped the reputation.",
    "defaultMode": "Precision applied to people instead of to text becomes correction, and colleagues remember being made small over a detail that did not change the outcome. Defending the wording past the point where anyone else cares acquires a reputation for pedantry that eclipses your judgment, and teams route drafts around you as a genuine loss to the work and to your standing.",
